<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104601" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρᾰφερός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέφω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well-fed, fat,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ τραφεροί</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ τραφερά</span> the <i>fat ones,</i> i. e.
			fishes, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				21.44
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> uses <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τραφερή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>), ἡ, as
				Subst., <i>dry land,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τραφερήν τε καὶ ὑγρήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.308
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				20.98
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				43
			</span></i>:—in later Poets as Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νομὸς τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					1027
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλευθος ὑγρή τε τ. τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.545
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἄρουρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					1.204
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤθεα τ.</span> tracts <i>of dry
				land,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.334
			</span></i>. (In this sense it is from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέφω</span> (A) <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i>make thick.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
